B-349 [new] `task prod:deploy` can ship stale `origin/main` silently — the release has no ship workflow, deploy has no dev↔main guard, and `/nc-status` + close-bar leg-1 are prod-blind — on 2026-09-02 `task prod:deploy` (run for the "Prod current and honest" milestone) rebuilt and returned `status:ok` while serving `origin/main`@`211c251` (the 2026-08-24 B2 cutover) because the `dev→main` merge was never done — `origin/main` was 103 commits / 9 days behind `dev`, found only by comparing prod `/api/v1/health` `git_sha` against `dev`. Four blind spots let it pass silently: (1) the merge/push half of the release was prose-only in the Taskfile (adjacent to B-348), so it's a skippable manual step; (2) `prod:deploy` had no guard that `origin/main` is current with `dev`, so it built stale main without complaint; (3) `task version` / close-bar leg-1 "parity" compares only the semver constants (`0.4.0`/`1.5.0`, unchanged across the 103 commits) → false-green "0 drift" on 9-day-stale prod; (4) `/nc-status` never inspects prod or compares `dev`↔`origin/main` (it reads planning files + `overnight-*` branch topology only), so it recommends "deploy next" with no awareness prod is stale or that a deploy already no-op'd. **Target-side half already fixed** on branch `tooling/prod-release-flow` (commit `a510aa0`, rides `ship-dev-to-main`): `task prod:ship` (guarded merge `origin/dev`→main + push), `task prod:release` (one-command ship+deploy), and a fail-loud stale-guard in `prod:deploy-backend` (refuses when `origin/dev` is ahead of `origin/main`; `ALLOW_STALE=1` overrides for a deliberate same-main rebuild). **Clone-side half remains** (graduates via the night-crew feedback loop / `design-findings-nightcrew.md`): `/nc-status` should compare `dev`↔`origin/main` and surface "prod N commits stale" as a first-class signal for deploying target repos, and the milestone close-bar leg-1 (parity) should assert `origin/dev is-ancestor-of origin/main` AND diff prod's live `/api/v1/health` `git_sha`, retiring the semver-only false-green. (attended deploy 2026-09-02 (prod shipped 9-day-old main; caught by prod git_sha vs dev)) · priority 20.5 — referenced by nothing · theme surfaced by 11 capture(s) across a cluster of 12 · 2d old
