B-22 [**✅ RESOLVED 2026-08-06 on `card/a2-harness-check-b` (commit `73547a0`, run `overnight-20260806`) — exactly the shape this lead specifies.** Check B now loops `for p in $DB_PKGS`, prints each package's exit status individually, and fails **naming every package that reported `ok`** — so the assertion is a conjunction over all seven rather than a disjunction that six reverts could satisfy. It **also asserts, as its own graded line, that it iterated `EXPECTED_DB_PKGS` (7)**, because `$DB_PKGS` is shared with Check B2 and silently trimming it would narrow both while both still printed PASS — the same defect one level up, so it is graded rather than trusted (`H1_DB_PKG_COUNT` overrides the constant to prove that assertion can go red). **Red demonstrated before the fix, not argued:** fail-loud was removed from six of the seven packages (`requested := dbURL != ""` → `requested := false` in the receipt/inventory/auth/purchasing `TestMain`s; `t.Fatal(testdb.Reason(…))` → `t.Skip(…)` in the recipes and sync helpers), leaving only `internal/workflow` honest; probing one by one read **1/0/0/0/0/0/0** while the aggregate check printed `PASS  go test exited 1`. The mutation was reverted — **no Go source is touched**, only `scripts/verify-test-harness.sh`. **Check B2 is deliberately unchanged** (the card's PARK trigger did not fire): its aggregate `-eq 0` is already a conjunction, so making B honest required no weakening of the over-correction guard. Cost is the live-server/missing-database DSN at ~0.02s per package — seven probes cost what one did; `H1_DEAD_PORT=1` stays opt-in. 🛑 **Status line written by `card/a4-gate-ladder`, not by A2** — A4 owns `BACKLOG.md` tonight, so A2 correctly left this entry alone; if A2's branch does not merge, this closure is false and must revert.] `verify-test-harness.sh` Check B aggregates with OR, so six of seven packages can report `ok` on a dropped database and the gate still prints PASS — the check runs one aggregate `cd backend && go test`, which is non-zero if *any* package fails, so reverting fail-loud in six of the seven converted packages (or in just `internal/inventory`) leaves `CHECK_B_AGGREGATE_EXIT=1` and the script reports harness OK with `ok github.com/yumyums/hq/internal/inventory 0.030s` sitting in a log it never reads. Only a 7-of-7 revert reds it. This is a stronger instance of the defect the card's own HANDOFF says it fixed in Check B2 — B2's unset direction genuinely aggregates AND across all seven. **The production fix is sound**: all seven packages exit 1 individually under three unreachable-DB shapes (dead port 110.7 s, unroutable host 109.7 s, live server / missing DB 0.02 s), so fail-loud does not depend on hanging. It is the guard that is weak. · _morning triage 2026-07-29 (T-28 decision 103a, adversarial finding F-1)_ (promoted → gate-harness-honesty (roadmap round 2026-08-05))
B-26 [**✅ RESOLVED 2026-08-06 — the residual is closed on `card/a4-gate-ladder` (run `overnight-20260806`).** The first half landed earlier: `.night-crew/knowledge/reference/gate-ladder.md` was written at triage 2026-08-03 (T-34 decision 138), and slates now cite that path in this repo rather than the phantom clone file. **What it left open, and this card closed, is the half this entry's own title names second:** the file recorded G1–G4 and G6 and **said nothing at all about G5**, so the gap survived as a silent question a future slate would re-ask. The ladder now carries §"🛑 There is no G5. The number is retired, not missing." — the ladder is **G1, G2 (Go), G2 (Playwright), G3, G4, G6, and that is the whole ladder**; do not invent a G5, do not renumber G6 down. It also records **where the number does survive, so neither sighting is mistaken for a gate**: the three hardening PRDs use "G5" for a *second independent enumeration pass* over user flows, and `reference/qa-coverage-findings-20260718.md` uses it as a *coverage-gap number* for a missing behavioural-oracle layer — two unrelated senses, neither ever run as a gate. Recorded as **retired-never-defined rather than renumbered**, exactly as this lead directs and per ledger decision 101. 🛑 **Not a park:** decision 101 already made this call at triage; the card executed a standing decision rather than legislating a new gate. Adding a real fifth gate — a new obligation on every future card — remains an operator call and would get a **name, not the number 5**. B-26's sibling finding **B-14 is now recorded in the same file** (that entry stays open — its remedy is clone-side).] The file every slate inherits gates G1–G6 from does not exist, and G5 has never been defined — every slate since 07-15 and every launch prompt say the gates are "unchanged from `reference/overnight-run-plan-20260707.md`". Confirmed by `find` at triage: **that file is nowhere in the repo.** The contract was recoverable from practice and the runs us