B-70 [**destination: next milestone** (tooling hygiene — cheap, and it protects gate evidence)] A raw NUL byte in `sync-rxdb/client.js` puts every `grep` into binary mode, so a gate grep returns nothing and reads as a pass — `sync-rxdb/client.js` contains exactly one NUL (`U+0000`), at byte offset 50850, deliberately: it is a delimiter inside a template literal, `scopeFingerprint(` + backtick + `${scopeIdentity(s)}<NUL>${serialized}` + backtick + `)`, chosen so the separator cannot occur in either operand. The technique is sound and the code is correct. **The side effect is not.** `file(1)` reports the file as `data`, and GNU grep switches to binary mode — so `grep -n 'export' sync-rxdb/client.js` **prints nothing and exits 1**, on a file containing 29 occurrences of `export`. Reproduced live at the start of card S1b: an early survey concluded `client.js` had no exports and no push path, both false, and the error was caught only because the conclusion was implausible enough to re-check with `grep -a`. 🛑 **The failure class is the one this repo keeps arming against:** several `done_when:` rows in this milestone are *"`grep -rn … ` returns nothing"*, and a `grep` that silently returns nothing because of a NUL byte is indistinguishable from a `grep` that returns nothing because the work is done. Any future gate grep whose scope includes `sync-rxdb/` is currently unreliable in the passing direction. · _run `20260803`, card S1b `sync-hard-cutover`, found by being wrong first_ (new)
