B-136 [done — `[FLD-16C]` in `tests/persistence.spec.js`, mutation-verified in both directions] The correction-photo camera path had zero executing coverage — B-65's other half — ✅ **RESOLVED 2026-08-03 at morning triage of run `overnight-20260804`, commit `70ea466`, branch `fix/correction-photo-coverage`.** `handleCorrectionPhotoCaptureClick` (`workflows.html:2129-2168`) is the byte-for-byte structural twin of the chain B-65 broke, and nothing executed it: `[FLD-CORRECTION-PHOTO]` covers the same slot but injects via `POST /saveResponse` — the transport bypass FLD-16B's own header names as "the blind spot B-65 lived in for months" — and `tests/workflows.spec.js:684-689` *reimplements* the production write inside `page.evaluate`, asserting against its own copy of the code. The suite's only `waitForEvent('filechooser')` was FLD-16B's, on the fail path. **Proved by mutation before the test existed:** planting the literal B-65 defect (`autoSaveField` at `:2154`) and running every photo/correction test returned **9 passed, rc=0**. `[FLD-16C]` now drives the real path (approver rejects with `require_photo` → presign + PUT stubbed at the network layer → hidden file input via filechooser) and reds on both mutations: `ReferenceError: autoSaveField is not defined`, and `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'value')` for the `resp.value || resp` form. 🛑 **The argument guard asserts the persisted bundle (`{_v: null, _correction_photo: <url>}`), NOT a checkbox state, and that was measured rather than chosen:** a first draft asserted the answer survived a back-and-reopen and failed, because `hydrateFieldState:1809` does `delete FIELD_RESPONSES[rej.field_id]` on **every** hydrate of a rejected submission ("uncheck a top-level field so crew must redo") — the test was wrong, not the code. No production code changed; `docs/data-flow-audit.md` row 8b corrected from an unqualified "OK". Footprint gate (`tests/workflows.spec.js tests/persistence.spec.js`, the `night-