B-157 [promoted → cdc-single-fire] One `/saveResponse` call fires any CDC trigger on `submission_responses` twice — `workflow/repository.go:826` (the save) plus `sync/ops.go:148` (`EmitOp`'s `UPDATE … SET lamport_ts` LWW stamp) are two row writes per user action, and a row-level trigger cannot tell them apart — so any change-data-capture mechanism on this table (spike C's LISTEN/NOTIFY relay included) sees 2× the write volume a reader would predict. Harmless in the spike only because the projection is an idempotent upsert; recorded beside the code in `spikec_relay.go`. (run `20260807-2` card C finding, morning triage 2026-08-07)
