B-172 [resolved 2026-08-25 — probe + health field + launcher banner + STORAGE_* rename landed on `feat/b2-storage` 2026-08-22; cutover code landed 2026-08-24 (`9f86f41`: last two x-amz-acl headers dropped with a no-ACL regression test, `POST /inventory/purchases/recover-receipts` Mercury re-fetch endpoint, `STORAGE_REQUIRED` startup gate); buckets `yumyums-hq-dev`/`yumyums-hq-prod` provisioned on `us-east-005` (public, keep-only-last-version lifecycle, per-env CORS via API) and dev smoke green (health `storage:ok`, raw PUT + anonymous GET); `toast/` archive restored to the prod bucket from sales-processor (uploaded=576 date-dirs, 20230825→20260816) — **cutover deployed to prod 2026-08-25** (`211c251`, backend 0.4.0 / frontend 1.5.0, health `storage:ok` through the tunnel); `.env.prod` STORAGE_* filled by operator, `task prod:deploy` clean; `recover-receipts` run 1 recovered 95/95 (0 missing, 0 failed) back to 2026-01-28. Follow-ups spun out: B-173 (unrecoverable onboarding videos + fail/correction photos), B-174 (sw-api-cache test reds), B-175 (worker attachment misindex)] Canceled DO Spaces account is invisible — startup logs a false-positive "presigner initialized", health says ok, storage death surfaces only as broken uploads/images — operator report 2026-08-22: the DigitalOcean account backing Spaces is canceled, yet the HQ app starts with no error anywhere. By construction nothing can notice: `backend/cmd/server/main.go:336-354` checks env-var *presence* only; `photos.NewSpacesClient` (`backend/internal/photos/spaces.go:24-31`) builds an offline S3 client from static creds (no network call); and `NewSpacesPresigner` has no error path at all — so with dead creds startup still logs `DO Spaces presigner initialized` (main.go:350), a false positive. Presigning is local HMAC, so the presign endpoints keep returning 200 URLs whose subsequent browser PUT fails against DO; the receipt worker's Spaces PUT failure only logs + falls back to Mercury URLs (`backend/internal/receipt/worker.go:384`); `/api/v1/health` (main.go:446-456) is a static `ok` with no storage field; and previously stored `digitaloceanspaces.com` public URLs (fail/correction photos, receipt images, onboarding videos) now render as broken media with no in-app surfacing. Data-exposure note: objects that lived only in the canceled bucket may already be unrecoverable — receipts persisted with the Mercury-URL fallback survive; direct Spaces uploads may not. (operator report 2026-08-22 (found while scoping the Backblaze B2 swap))
