B-175 [promoted → receipt-worker-correctness] Receipt worker misindexes attachments after a failed download — ext/filename taken from the wrong attachment — `runIngestCycle`'s download loop appends to `blobs` while skipping failed downloads, then the upload loop indexes `tx.Attachments[i]` by blob index (`worker.go` download/upload loops) — after any skip, every later blob pairs with the wrong attachment's `FileName`/`URL`, so extensions and Mercury-fallback URLs shift by one. Latent until a multi-attachment tx has a partial download failure. The B-172 recovery path (`recoverOneTx`) deliberately avoids the pattern (all-or-nothing per tx); the live ingest path still carries it. (B-172 cutover code review 2026-08-24)
